1. Posting notes:
Job title: Artificial Intelligence, Data, & Machine Learning Engineering Undergraduate Internship
Industry / company type: Technology and data science within a global athletic-apparel and sports company.
Approximate seniority: Undergraduate / entry-level intern; 10-week paid internship.

Eligibility and application qualifications
•	Listed qualification: Enrolled in a bachelor’s degree program with expected graduation between December 2027 and Spring 2028.
•	Listed qualification: Background in computer science, mathematics, statistics, or a related technical field.
•	Listed qualification: 0–2 years of work experience.
•	Preferred: Resume submission in PDF format is “strongly preferred”; the wording does not make PDF a hard requirement.

Core technical skills (listed outside the “Preferred Technical Skills” subsection)
•	Knowledge of Python, SQL, and Tableau.
•	Knowledge of AI/ML techniques, with neural networks, tree ensembles, and regressions as examples.
•	Knowledge of data structures and algorithms.
•	Proficiency in solution and technical design.
•	Strong problem-solving, debugging, testing, and analysis skills.
•	Ability to learn new programming languages, technologies, and frameworks quickly.

Explicitly preferred technical skills
•	Demonstrated interest in using Generative AI to improve development/data-science workflows or implementing enterprise Generative AI solutions.
•	Awareness of data-science platforms such as Databricks or SageMaker, distributed engines such as Spark, AWS cloud, CI/CD pipelines, and containerization.
•	Ability to communicate technical topics in written, oral, and visual forms to peers and explain solution benefits and trade-offs.

Additional expectations implied by the role description (not a separate formal requirements list)
•	Think critically, work with disparate or messy datasets, and help design complex solutions end to end.
•	Contribute to applied AI/ML research and development, including taking technologies toward production use; own a scoped project and collaborate with experienced teammates.
•	Keep learning and share knowledge. Example project areas include incident detection, computer vision, robotics, sustainability, and accessible AI.

2. Posting notes:
Job title: Data Science Intern (Summer 2027)
Industry / company type: Automotive energy storage and battery manufacturing / sustainability.
Approximate seniority: Undergraduate / entry-level summer intern; up to 40 hours per week.

Eligibility qualifications listed under “What We Look For”
•	Currently enrolled as a full-time student at an accredited U.S. college or university.
•	Pursuing an undergraduate degree in Data Science.
•	Able to be in the greater Milwaukee area during summer 2027.
•	Available for the Summer 2027 internship, up to 40 hours per week.
